From fca629cf016d75ce60ba1a4e540aedc3df889542 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:56:48 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 82/90] render: perspective layers and particles in
 orthographic scenes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

An orthographic scene's `perspective` image and text layers (object flag 0x80 at +0x120, setter
FUN_1401ca270) and its perspective particle systems (flags bit 2) are drawn by WE through the
scene's perspective camera (GH 0x1401b4fd0, called from the image draw GH 0x140214b50 and the
particle render GH 0x14025bc30): fov = general.perspectiveoverridefov (+0x144, default 95 — the
camera update GH 0x1401b8af0 takes it as the effective fov when the ortho flag is set), the eye on
the view's axis at d = (height / 2) / tan (fov / 2) (= −1 / (tan (fov / 2) · proj[1][1])), near
5, far max (15000, d + 1000). So z 0 lands where the orthographic camera puts it, and a layer's
own x/y angles and z (WE's object matrix) show.

LWE ignored both keys: such layers were flat (no z, no x/y turn), and perspective particles had
general.fov from an eye at z 1000 (z 0 drawn 1.16 x at fov 50). The view's zoom and shake apply
as to the orthographic view. `perspective` is an IEffectLayer property (registered, live).
Inferred: the parents' x/y angles are not followed (the 2D transform resolves z turns only);
full-screen and compose layers keep covering the screen.

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/spikes/we-coverage.md F5 (G20 perspectiveoverridefov, G21/E43 perspective)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
